// CORPORATE KOMBAT — BONUS STAGE — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CORPORATE KOMBAT as a real chiptune arrangement — written for a console's channels the way an
// NES / Game Boy composer would have, not the song swapped onto chip sounds (that is office-8bit).
// A game alternate of office, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk.
// 
// Peter: "a couple of remixes of this now. Chiptune I think for one... Surprise me!!"
// 
// PULSE 1   MELODY A, note for note as office.js plays it, at the verse's octave on a 25% pulse:
//           fast delayed vibrato, the office's overlaps as legato slides, a whole-step grace scoop
//           (lead3) on the long notes of the chorus and climax. The B melody on 12.5%; the counter
//           and the wind-down on a sweeping-duty PWM pulse (the C64 lead); the lobby on a 50% vibes square.
// PULSE 2   the NES echo (the hook a dotted eighth later on 12.5%, 9 dB down) in the verse, floor 23,
//           the counter, B again and the wind-down; a twin lead a third under in the chorus and the
//           ending; the office's slide-guitar answer in the first B; the hook an octave up in the
//           climax; every pitch sweep (up into 9, 17 and 45, down into 37).
// ARP       the chords as a 1/32 three-note arpeggio (noteFx arp) on a flat 50% square; brass stabs
//           as arp stabs in floor 23; a 1/16 wave-channel (triangle) arp in the lobby, counter, wind-down.
// TRIANGLE  office's disco octave bass note for note, an octave up on a flat-gated triangle; office's
//           sine sub under its roots for the low end.
// NOISE     the NES kit (a longer triangle-drop kick), pocket-pixel ghosts and shaker, triangle tom
//           bloops in the fills, the console's pulse zap on the downbeats, a noise riser into 29 and 45.
// 
// The form and harmony are office's: 115 BPM, swing 55, 60 bars, the lobby once, the loop 5–52.
// Harmony beat by beat as its DX comp voices it, with a passing chord on the last sixteenth
// wherever its bass walks in chromatically, so the arp follows the walk. The climax (45–52) lifts a
// whole step to A minor, pivoting D7 → E7 in bar 44 and coming home inside bar 52 (Dm, then D).
// Five channels at most at any moment; the generator asserts one lane a channel at a time.
// 
//   1–4    LOBBY (G major, once; the cabinet screen loops it through the lobby speaker) — the vibes hook on a decaying 50% square, its echo on 12.5%, a 1/16 wave arp (triangle), a tresillo triangle bass, pocket shaker, clave and conga blips
//   5–8    DOORS OPEN (G minor) — the triangle disco bass and sine sub, the 1/32 arp on Gm7 · B♭ · Cm7 · Gm/D, the NES kit four on the floor with a rim blip on 2 and 4; a snare run, tom bloops and a pulse sweep up into
//   9–16   VERSE — MELODY A on the 25% pulse, the dotted-eighth echo on 12.5%; the rim blip becomes the noise snare at 13; a stutter on 12.3–4 (the office's own spot); tom cascade and a sweep into
//   17–24  CHORUS — the hook with grace scoops on its long notes and the 50% twin-lead a third under it; 16th hats, open hats, Game Boy ghosts, crash and zap
//   25–28  B — the B melody thin on 12.5%; pulse 2 plays the office's slide-guitar answer with chip portamento; the noise riser from 27, a noise roll into
//   29–36  FLOOR 23 — the hook and its echo; the arp turns into stabs in the brass's rhythm; the triangle takes the office's floor-23 bass feature; a falling sweep and toms into
//   37–40  COUNTER — the office's long-note counter-melody on the sweeping-duty PWM pulse (the C64 lead) with its echo, over the 1/16 wave arp
//   41–44  B AGAIN — 12.5% and its echo; the riser; 44 pivots D7 → E7, a stutter and a sweep up into
//   45–52  CLIMAX, A MINOR — the hook up a whole step with its graces, pulse 2 an octave above (the office's own register); full kit; 52 comes home: Dm, then D, tom cascade into the loop at 5
//   53–56  WIND-DOWN (after the loop) — the office's wind-down melody on the PWM pulse with its echo, E♭ Cm7 Am7♭5 D7, half-time noise
//   57–60  ENDING — the hook with the twin lead; the D7 hits as arp stabs with the snare; G6/9: the held G, the lobby's vibes arpeggio, the crash
// 
// Trailing master gain -3.3 dB.
// 60 bars at 115, 125 s. Generator: work/local/_office-remix-bonus-stage.mjs.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
